for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T23:21:45-07:00","id":1310221,"title":"","content":"So.<br /> <br /> Saw Endgame.<br /> <br /> I hate to admit it, but I really enjoyed that. That was hella cathartic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-05T23:48:57-07:00","id":1310225,"title":"","content":"So, kick to things off since this IS the spoiler thread...<br /> <br /> While yes, the time travel logic established in the movie is iffy regarding Cap's ultimate fate, personally I say...<br /> <br /> Guys. Let him have his happy ending. He earned it, dammit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T00:29:31-07:00","id":1310232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310225#post1310225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, kick to things off since this IS the spoiler thread...<br /> <br /> While yes, the time travel logic established in the movie is iffy regarding Cap's ultimate fate, personally I say...<br /> <br /> Guys. Let him have his happy ending. He earned it, dammit.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing about being apathetic towards that franchise-I realized that was a nit to pick but just couldn't care.<br /> <br /> Gotta admit, I'm surprised he lived and Stark didn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T00:51:58-07:00","id":1310239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310232#post1310232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing about being apathetic towards that franchise-I realized that was a nit to pick but just couldn't care.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, my corner of the internet is a lot more enthusiastic about this sort of thing (and staunchly believes &quot;superhero fatigue&quot; has no objective data and merit to be worth discussing), so kinda hard for me to avoid it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gotta admit, I'm surprised he lived and Stark didn't. </div> </div> </div>I'm ok with things.<br /> <br /> I was personally in the camp that they were going to go for an &quot;everybody&quot; or &quot;nobody&quot; outcome: either ALL of the original Avengers were going to die, or NONE of them were, and they would just be conveniently side-lined. Instead Marvel/Disney went for...some lived, some died, some are permanently retired.<br /> <br /> Am looking forward to Thor with the Guardians in GotGvol3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T09:51:05-07:00","id":1310306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310239#post1310239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, my corner of the internet is a lot more enthusiastic about this sort of thing (and staunchly believes &quot;superhero fatigue&quot; has no objective data and merit to be worth discussing), so kinda hard for me to avoid it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm ok with things.<br /> <br /> I was personally in the camp that they were going to go for an &quot;everybody&quot; or &quot;nobody&quot; outcome: either ALL of the original Avengers were going to die, or NONE of them were, and they would just be conveniently side-lined. Instead Marvel/Disney went for...some lived, some died, some are permanently retired.<br /> <br /> Am looking forward to Thor with the Guardians in GotGvol3.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thor in the Guardians is a brilliant move and I cannot wait.<br /> <br /> I was okay with Steve's breach too, because that catharsis has been earned and at some point you gotta throw your hands up and go &quot;Fuck it, have it&quot; and we well and reached that point. Stark's death is a little more bitter, because I ended up wanting him to go back to his little house and farm? But On the other hand, ending on the words that started this whole thing was more of a right move than I expected.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-06-2019, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:45:18-07:00","id":1310328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310306#post1310306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was okay with Steve's breach too, because that catharsis has been earned at some point you gotta throw your hands up and go &quot;Fuck it, have it&quot; and we well and reached that point. Stark's death is a little more bitter, because I ended up wanting him to go back to his little house and farm? But On the other hand, ending on the words that started this whole thing was more of a right move than I expected.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just felt that move coming. The moment I saw him with the Gems after the Thanos line I was like &quot;he's gonna say it&quot;. Being the one in my group that had to drag my friends to see Iron Man because I was the &quot;comics guy&quot; of the group, with Tony always having been one of my favorites, it hit me hard.<br /> <br /> I have my share of criticism for this movie, but that moment was cathartic beyond belief and a majestic reminder of all the road done so far and how things change. Cultural zeitgeist in four words, worth paying for the movie all by itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 05-06-2019, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T11:45:26-07:00","id":1310329,"title":"","content":"I suppose it would have felt a little bit same-y if Tony and Clint were depicted as having happily gone back to their family.<br /> <br /> ...which even then I was kinda surprised they gave the outcome they did with Tony in the 5 Years Later since with the whole &quot;family in a private house in the rural nowhere&quot;, weren't they just repeating what Clint got?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T12:02:11-07:00","id":1310337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310329#post1310329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose it would have felt a little bit same-y if Tony and Clint were depicted as having happily gone back to their family.<br /> <br /> ...which even then I was kinda surprised they gave the outcome they did with Tony in the 5 Years Later since with the whole &quot;family in a private house in the rural nowhere&quot;, weren't they just repeating what Clint got?</div> </div> </div> </div>Different contexts, with the notation of how Tony <i>got</i> the idea for wanting that from his time visiting Barton's family in Ultron. It was actually a really good pen-ultimate step to his final actualization, the completion of his arc, because he arrived on the opposite side of where he started and had to confront the Iron Man choice all over again, but this time with more wisdom and clarity. The backdrop of the Snap is also important for the context, because Barton's schtick represents sort of equanmity that Stark's life(Both in Iron Man 1 and here) doesn't present. Stark demonstrates a willingness to make it all about himself again(for different) reasons, and has to step up and out into his heroism.<br /> <br /> EDIT: It also retreads Tony's willingness to &quot;cut the wire&quot; rather than &quot;lay down on the wire&quot; in a more mature context, because throughout the series, Tony's answers have been to try and fix the way things are, to cheat the systems in place for his ideals, and even if he has lain on the wire before, this was the final extension of that conversation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-06-2019, 03:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T12:03:19-07:00","id":1310338,"title":"","content":"I thought it was a fun movie, and it even had a few moments I thought were really moving. That said, I feel ambivalent about how invested you have to be in the MCU to really *get* this movie.<br /> <br /> I don't normally see movies in theaters - I prefer to watch them at home, so I can eat healthy snacks that aren't overpriced and snark at the movie without bothering anyone. But I thought it would be better to see Endgame still in theaters, partly for the full audiovisual experience and partly so I wouldn't have to dodge spoilers for the next several months until it came out for streaming services and DVD.<br /> <br /> I was mostly caught up on Marvel movies - the only important one I hadn't seen was Captain Marvel, because it's still in theaters. So I went to see Captain Marvel last Saturday, and Endgame the day after. And I'm glad I did, because it turns out that Captain Marvel is moderately important to Endgame, and if I didn't have her background the parts of the movie where she turns up would have been much less impactful, if not actually confusing.<br /> <br /> That got me thinking - you really have to have seen almost every Marvel movie to fully appreciate Endgame. Fans of the comics can maybe skip a few, but otherwise you're looking at 18-21 movies just to <i>comprehend</i> all of what is happening in Endgame. And that feels like a lot to ask from casual moviegoers.<br /> <br /> The list of said movies, going all the way back to 2008:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (The titles in bold are necessities; the ones in italics may be optional.)<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Man</b><br /> <b>The Incredible Hulk</b><br /> <i>Iron Man 2</i><br /> <b>Thor</b><br /> <b>Captain America: The First Avenger</b><br /> <b>The Avengers</b><br /> <i>Iron Man 3</i><br /> <b>Thor: The Dark World<br /> Captain America: The Winter Soldier</b><br /> <b>Guardians of the Galaxy<br /> Avengers: Age of Ultron<br /> Ant-Man<br /> Captain America: Civil War<br /> Doctor Strange</b><br /> <i>Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2</i><br /> <b>Spiderman: Homecoming<br /> Thor: Ragnarok</b><br /> <b>Black Panther<br /> Avengers: Infinity War<br /> Ant-Man and the Wasp</b><br /> <b>Captain Marvel</b><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 05-06-2019, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-06T12:58:26-07:00","id":1310355,"title":"","content":"No, this movie exists to reward people who have been along for the ride. I imagine <i>I </i>would like seeing this without context, because my <i>usual</i> way of finding out things is coming in the middle of everything (The first episode of Game of Thrones I ever watched was the Battle of Winterfell and I had a lot of fun not knowing anything about anything but still getting into the drama presented), but hell if <i>anyone</i> could just do that.<br /> <br /> And honestly, one of the problems of the movie is that it delivers very little outside of the catharsis for people who have been along for the ride. It's thematic core isn't all that strong or terribly developed(But damn is it said with feeling), there's not a whole lot of work to get you into it the characters on the virtue of this film, and so much of it needs an explanation for anyone who hasn't been there.<br /> <br /> And that's really the whole gamble of the franchise, isn't it? They promise grand stories that you need all the chapters on in order to get the big payout at the end, and if you don't, you're gonna be lost, so you watch all of them just to not miss out and oh hey, if you pick up a new favorite, that's a branch you'll come back around for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T00:44:40-07:00","id":1310495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310338#post1310338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was a fun movie, and it even had a few moments I thought were really moving. That said, I feel ambivalent about how invested you have to be in the MCU to really *get* this movie.<br /> <br /> I don't normally see movies in theaters - I prefer to watch them at home, so I can eat healthy snacks that aren't overpriced and snark at the movie without bothering anyone. But I thought it would be better to see Endgame still in theaters, partly for the full audiovisual experience and partly so I wouldn't have to dodge spoilers for the next several months until it came out for streaming services and DVD.<br /> <br /> I was mostly caught up on Marvel movies - the only important one I hadn't seen was Captain Marvel, because it's still in theaters. So I went to see Captain Marvel last Saturday, and Endgame the day after. And I'm glad I did, because it turns out that Captain Marvel is moderately important to Endgame, and if I didn't have her background the parts of the movie where she turns up would have been much less impactful, if not actually confusing.<br /> <br /> That got me thinking - you really have to have seen almost every Marvel movie to fully appreciate Endgame. Fans of the comics can maybe skip a few, but otherwise you're looking at 18-21 movies just to <i>comprehend</i> all of what is happening in Endgame. And that feels like a lot to ask from casual moviegoers.<br /> <br /> The list of said movies, going all the way back to 2008:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> (The titles in bold are necessities; the ones in italics may be optional.)<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Man</b><br /> <b>The Incredible Hulk</b><br /> <i>Iron Man 2</i><br /> <b>Thor</b><br /> <b>Captain America: The First Avenger</b><br /> <b>The Avengers</b><br /> <i>Iron Man 3</i><br /> <b>Thor: The Dark World<br /> Captain America: The Winter Soldier</b><br /> <b>Guardians of the Galaxy<br /> Avengers: Age of Ultron<br /> Ant-Man<br /> Captain America: Civil War<br /> Doctor Strange</b><br /> <i>Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2</i><br /> <b>Spiderman: Homecoming<br /> Thor: Ragnarok</b><br /> <b>Black Panther<br /> Avengers: Infinity War<br /> Ant-Man and the Wasp</b><br /> <b>Captain Marvel</b><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u2019t think all that context is as necessary as it seems to someone who has it. Out of your list, I\u2019ve only seen Iron Man 1, 2, and 3, Thor, The Avengers, Guardians of the Galaxy, Age of Ultron, Civil War, Spiderman, and Infinity War. Now, that\u2019s a fair number of movies still, but I skipped a <i>lot</i> of the \u201cessential\u201d ones, and I think I could have skipped a few more and still been able to follow it. Honestly, I think if you\u2019ve seen Infinity War, you can get Endgame, and to get Infinity War, you only really need to have seen Avengers, Ultron, and Civil War. The movies themselves and pop culture osmosis will get you the rest of the way. Will you appreciate the movies as much as the folks who have seen all the other movies that set them up? No, of course not. But the films are constructed well enough and culturally relevant enough that you can still understand them without all that context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T10:34:21-07:00","id":1310570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310355#post1310355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree 100%. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310495#post1310495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think all that context is as necessary as it seems to someone who has it. Out of your list, I\u2019ve only seen Iron Man 1, 2, and 3, Thor, The Avengers, Guardians of the Galaxy, Age of Ultron, Civil War, Spiderman, and Infinity War. Now, that\u2019s a fair number of movies still, but I skipped a <i>lot</i> of the \u201cessential\u201d ones, and I think I could have skipped a few more and still been able to follow it. Honestly, I think if you\u2019ve seen Infinity War, you can get Endgame, and to get Infinity War, you only really need to have seen Avengers, Ultron, and Civil War. The movies themselves and pop culture osmosis will get you the rest of the way. Will you appreciate the movies as much as the folks who have seen all the other movies that set them up? No, of course not. But the films are constructed well enough and culturally relevant enough that you can still understand them without all that context.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I may paraphrase: <br /> &quot;I've only seen 10 previous movies, and I was able to follow the 11th one just fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I think you only really need to have seen 4 previous movies to get the 5th one.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's a difference in scale, but you're still describing the same problem: Avengers: Endgame is the culmination of a lengthy series of films, and requires familiarity with those films to fully enjoy. This is how <a href=\"https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ContinuityLockOut\" target=\"_blank\">continuity lockout</a> happens. <br /> <br /> Maybe that wouldn't be so much of a problem <i>except </i>you <a href=\"https://www.cnet.com/how-to/avengers-endgame-countdown-stream-marvel-movies-in-order/\" target=\"_blank\">can't just stream all of the movies</a>, like you can episodes of Game of Thrones or many other present-day serials. Marvel/Disney have successfully transported the production model that made Marvel's comics successful for generations* to the silver screen, but they haven't provided a modern solution to the age-old problem of helping those who aren't &quot;true believers&quot; get in on the action. Youtube rentals and the like can take up the slack, but that's not ideal. <br /> <br /> * Make a bunch of individual series with their own continuities; give those series little tie-ins to each other to encourage fans of one series to buy others; have big crossover events every so often that <b>heavily</b> encourage investment in multiple series; profit from both the little fish who mainly devour one series and the whales who try to swallow it all. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-07T12:08:58-07:00","id":1310594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1310570#post1310570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I may paraphrase: <br /> &amp;quot;I've only seen 10 previous movies, and I was able to follow the 11th one just fine.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;I think you only really need to have seen 4 previous movies to get the 5th one.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> There's a difference in scale, but you're still describing the same problem: Avengers: Endgame is the culmination of a lengthy series of films, and requires familiarity with those films to fully enjoy. This is how <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/ContinuityLockOut&amp;quot;]continuity</a> lockout[/URL] happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, absolutely. I agree that\u2019s a real issue, I just thought it worth pointing out that the required investment is not as big as it may look. Still not ideal, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:12:35-07:00","id":1310856,"title":"","content":"Alright what else was there...<br /> <br /> So Captain Marvel got kind of shafted and oversold.<br /> <br /> Contrary to Feige &amp; Co's marketing overhype and bluster about her being the strongest Avenger and how much of a huge get to our main cast in the fight against Thanos she's...not really in the movie that much. She pops up in the beginning and participates in the climactic battle but otherwise, nothing else. Not to say that she doesn't make any meaningful impacts on the plot, because she does: she's the one who rescues Tony and Nebula at the beginning, and she is the one who takes out Thanos' warship...but that's about it. And personally, those tasks could have been done by anyone else or achieved in a different way. She doesn't even participate in the Time-Heist.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, the issue people were fearing about Carol solo-ing Thanos and upstaging all of the other Avengers that we've followed and grown to care about doesn't happen...it's just the exact opposite where she's barely a blip in the movie's radar.<br /> <br /> (also personally, I thought her solo movie was just...ok. nothing spectacular about it, just &quot;ok&quot;)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-08T18:42:05-07:00","id":1310865,"title":"","content":"Felt the same about her movie, and honestly, the way they played her was the correct answer. She definitely has punchy appearances, but considering the main arcs to fulfill, anything more than some strong, brief appearances would have been narraitively unsatisfying, and barring three films, I don't think I could ever really accuse Marvel of dropping the ball.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T22:37:23-07:00","id":1311161,"title":"","content":"Random thoughts:<br /> <br /> I enjoyed it quite a bit, and felt it was a good ending to a decade long saga. Especially touching, for me, was Thor getting to see his mom again. Also cool to see human Jarvis again.<br /> <br /> The I am Iron Man line isn't just a call back to the first film, but to its initial trailer and its use of the Black Sabbath song as well, which is kind of meta.<br /> <br /> My minor irks: The didn't bring Quicksilver back (I've been a big fan of the character since Peter David's run on X-Factor way back when), and Hank Pym and Janet van Dyne weren't in the final battle as was apparently originally planned (getting to see Bill Foster as Goliath would've been nice too).<br /> <br /> Predictions going forward:<br /> <br /> In Spiderman: FFH, <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">everything the trailer is leading you to believe is a lie. Mystero is not from another earth and the Nick Fury Spiderman meets is an imposter, because that is Mysterio's entire shtick. Even more so if the Chameleon turns out to be in the film as well. </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Kang the Conquerer will be the next major franchise villian, including his various incarnations as Immortus, Scarlet Centurian, and Pharaoh Rama Tut. Likely attracted by the time travel and its possible disruptions.<br /> <br /> The next Black Panther movie will be subtitled War of Kings and have him battle Namor.<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Galaxy 3 will focus on finding past-Gamora and when they do, she'll be with Adam Warlock, Pip the Troll, and Moondragon. Also at least some sort of inclusion of Beta Ray Bill, since Thor will be there (and maybe a return of Sif).<br /> <br /> Ant-Man 3 will have his daughter Cassie become Stature, and hopefully include the villian Goliath and female Yellow Jacket.<br /> <br /> They will do a Falcon-Cap film that draws on the Truth story for ideas, and will introduce Patriot as Sam's new protoge.<br /> <br /> There will be a Young Avengers film that will include Stature, Patriot, either Marvel Boy or Ms Marvel, Wiccan, Hulkling, Shuri, and Vision resurrected by Shuri but his mind and personality incomplete and reduced to adolescence.<br /> <br /> Ross will recruit Bucky to lead a Thunderbolts team in their own film, with a team including Ghost and possibly Zemo.<br /> <br /> We will get a Fantastic Four film, possibly an X-Men reboot, and at some point, see the introduction of SheHulk.<br /> <br /> Such are my predictions, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T22:43:58-07:00","id":1311162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311161#post1311161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They will do a Falcon-Cap film that draws on the Truth story for ideas, and will introduce Patriot as Sam's new protoge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah about that...<br /> <br /> There is an exclusive streaming show coming to Disney+ called &quot;Falcon and Winter Soldier&quot;. So any further adventures of the two are happening there and not in the movies.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T12:15:58-07:00","id":1311263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311162#post1311162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah about that...<br /> <br /> There is an exclusive streaming show coming to Disney+ called &quot;Falcon and Winter Soldier&quot;. So any further adventures of the two are happening there and not in the movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like the title of a 1970s sitcom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Why am I picturing Disney trying to do some sort of superhero version of a buddy cop show? But I still think such a show is likely to mine Truth for some plots and characters at some point. It would be cool if they get to fight the Serpent Society.<br /> <br /> (I'm a little disappointed that there is no way they'll subtitle it Team America and eventually work in Nomad, US Agent, Battlestar, Jack Flag, Free Spirit, Golden Girl, Patriot, Citizen V, American Eagle, Black Crow, and others. But then I'm the sort of weirdo who liked D-Man and thought he'd actually be a good subject for a Netflix series.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T12:27:17-07:00","id":1311265,"title":"","content":"I mean, there's no way it's <i>not</i> a superhero buddy cop series.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-10T14:10:39-07:00","id":1311284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311265#post1311265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, there's no way it's <i>not</i> a superhero buddy cop series.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. <br /> <br /> Will Sharon Carter be in it, I wonder? <br /> <br /> I admit I'm very unlikely to sign up for Disney's new service at this point, but if they do a Luke Cage crossover where Nightshade turns Sam and/or Bucky into werewolves, I will have no choice but to pay money to see that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T00:02:55-07:00","id":1311353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311284#post1311284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I admit I'm very unlikely to sign up for Disney's new service at this point, but if they do a <b>Luke Cage</b> crossover where Nightshade turns Sam and/or Bucky into werewolves, I will have no choice but to pay money to see that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah about that...<br /> <br /> By all accounts, it was apparently Netflix's call to cancel the Marvel-Netflix shows, and not Disney/Marvel's. Meaning that they are open to bringing them back...one problem though. There's apparently a clause in the legal work that prevents any of the cancelled projects to appear on a non-Netflix platform until 2 years have elapsed after cancellation.<br /> <br /> So if they wanted to restart things with those shows it's going to be a bit...nvm that the actors and creators involved would have probably already moved on to other projects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T08:13:53-07:00","id":1311383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311353#post1311353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah about that...<br /> <br /> By all accounts, it was apparently Netflix's call to cancel the Marvel-Netflix shows, and not Disney/Marvel's. Meaning that they are open to bringing them back...one problem though. There's apparently a clause in the legal work that prevents any of the cancelled projects to appear on a non-Netflix platform until 2 years have elapsed after cancellation.<br /> <br /> So if they wanted to restart things with those shows it's going to be a bit...nvm that the actors and creators involved would have probably already moved on to other projects.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say not only moved on to other projects. but Disney also have an image to maintain and having something like Daredevil and Luke Cage on their would be very cross to that. The Netflix shows had a more adult take on the normal MCU.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T13:56:36-07:00","id":1311432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311353#post1311353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah about that...<br /> <br /> By all accounts, it was apparently Netflix's call to cancel the Marvel-Netflix shows, and not Disney/Marvel's. Meaning that they are open to bringing them back...one problem though. There's apparently a clause in the legal work that prevents any of the cancelled projects to appear on a non-Netflix platform until 2 years have elapsed after cancellation.<br /> <br /> So if they wanted to restart things with those shows it's going to be a bit...nvm that the actors and creators involved would have probably already moved on to other projects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why must you tell me things that make me cry? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-11T14:38:40-07:00","id":1311440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311432#post1311432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why must you tell me things that make me cry? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/teepublic/image/private/s--t-nKXJ-2--/t_Resized%20Artwork/c_fit,g_north_west,h_954,w_954/co_36538b,e_outline:35/co_36538b,e_outline:inner_fill:35/co_ffffff,e_outline:35/co_ffffff,e_outline:inner_fill:35/co_bbbbbb,e_outline:3:1000/c_mpad,g_center,h_1260,w_1260/b_rgb:eeeeee/c_limit,f_jpg,h_630,q_90,w_630/v1540508033/production/designs/3388381_0.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T08:51:26-07:00","id":1311562,"title":"","content":"A lot of folks are predicting that Mysterio is lying about alternate universes and that Kang is going to be the next big villain, but I don\u2019t see it. Alternate universes would be a great way to bring the Fantastic 4 and X-Men into the MCU without wasting time on origin stories we\u2019ve already seen a million times or raising questions of why they didn\u2019t help with Thanos. Plus, how can you raise the stakes from a villain who succeeded in killing half the universe and when the heroes brought the dead back, set out to destroy the whole universe? The only way, in my opinion, to follow Thanos that wouldn\u2019t feel like a let down in comparison is with a villain who poses a threat to multiple universes. I don\u2019t think Kang the Conqueror fits that bill. I see him as the villain of <i>an</i> Avengers movie, a-la Age of Ultron. I think the next Thanos-level franchise villain will be Doctor Doom, in an MCU take on Secret Wars. But, as with the Infinity saga, I think it\u2019s going to take them several years to build up to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T09:49:54-07:00","id":1311576,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think the alternate universe bit is absolutely true. It works too well as a way to integrate the Fox properties. I just think that Mysterio is lying about being a hero because... Mysterio. Like, that was literally his first plotline in the comics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T11:28:01-07:00","id":1311589,"title":"","content":"I have feelings about Doom and wish he could take his spot as Marvel's top villain even in the MCU, but at this point I can't imagine it being easy (provided it happens at all).<br /> <br /> Properly done, Doom can give a lot to the MCU (not to mention that &quot;dark mirror to Iron Man&quot; angle which sometimes pops up in the comics would do wonders here), but that would require time, patience and careful execution.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure they'll do that, to be honest. Not because they can't, they have all the skills, but I don't think the desire to do it is there. We'll see. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T14:46:02-07:00","id":1311612,"title":"","content":"I think they are definitely going to have another big villain for the MCU. After how incredibly successful Avengers was, there's no doubt that they are going to want to replicate it but they'll need a solid villain for the next capstone to their ensemble movie.<br /> <br /> Doom seems like a pretty solid choice for that role as he was always one of the most iconic Marvel villains. Of course there are plenty other big villains they could focus for the MCU as well. For example it wouldn't be hard to say, &quot;Galactus sensed the vast energy spike from the Infinity Gems on Earth and is heading towards Earth to devour the planet.&quot; I also suspect that at some point we're going to see a House of M inspired storyline based around Scarlet Witch and her attempt to twist reality to bring back Vision.<br /> <br /> As for Doom it wouldn't be too hard to set him up in the new movies. Just say he and the Fantastic Four were engaged in quantum research (after how important it turned out to be in the last movie it would be no surprise to see a lot of people experimenting with it). The Fantastic Four get super powers and Doom gets stuck in the quantum Realm for an extended period of time. When he eventually returns, he's been warped by the Quantum Realm and has access to &quot;magical powers&quot; (which were also a core component of his character alongside his technological expertise).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-12-2019, 05:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T16:04:47-07:00","id":1311625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1311612#post1311612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they are definitely going to have another big villain for the MCU. After how incredibly successful Avengers was, there's no doubt that they are going to want to replicate it but they'll need a solid villain for the next capstone to their ensemble movie.<br /> <br /> Doom seems like a pretty solid choice for that role as he was always one of the most iconic Marvel villains. Of course there are plenty other big villains they could focus for the MCU as well. For example it wouldn't be hard to say, &quot;Galactus sensed the vast energy spike from the Infinity Gems on Earth and is heading towards Earth to devour the planet.&quot; I also suspect that at some point we're going to see a House of M inspired storyline based around Scarlet Witch and her attempt to twist reality to bring back Vision.<br /> <br /> As for Doom it wouldn't be too hard to set him up in the new movies. Just say he and the Fantastic Four were engaged in quantum research (after how important it turned out to be in the last movie it would be no surprise to see a lot of people experimenting with it). The Fantastic Four get super powers and Doom gets stuck in the quantum Realm for an extended period of time. When he eventually returns, he's been warped by the Quantum Realm and has access to &quot;magical powers&quot; (which were also a core component of his character alongside his technological expertise).</div> </div> </div> </div>Please no, I hate when they try to give Doom powers. it just cheapens him.Just make his origin the same as in the comics. Hates Reed, study magic and technology, and wants to rescue his mom's soul from hell. I would introduce him in Dr. Strange or FF 2. build him up and give him room to breathe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","user":"Grimmi05","date":". 05-12-2019, 07:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24179-grimmi05","name":"Grimmi05","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-12T16:06:45-07:00","id":1311626,"title":"","content":"Although... If Marvel does want to put a heroic spin on Mysterio, you know what would be great? Do the twist reveal that he's been the villain all along, but interacting with Spiderman has swayed him a bit. Not enough that it avoids the blowout fight at the end, but Mysterio is repentant afterwards. Cut to the stinger and Mysterio is in prison, trying to be better, but needing support. Someone approaches him (maybe Fury, Hawkeye, General Ross, or even Norman freaking Osborn) and says that the Avengers saved the world, but they aren't enough. A new team is being put together, a team of people who have done bad things (hence Hawkeye being a possible sponser) but want to turn their lives around. If Mysterio joins the team, they'll get him out on early parole. <br /> <br /> That team is the Thunderbolts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-13T00:50:59-07:00","id":1311724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin<