?p=1313908#post1313908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think arrogance has been a key personality trait of Tony Stark's going back at least into the late 70s when I started reading his comics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Depends on the writer, but as with everything, there are levels to it. Stark in the 616 was really never as dismissive and arrogant to the same degree he is portrayed in the MU. Busiek always wrote him as confident and sometimes even a bit cocky, but never to the 'asshole' degree he's been shown at times to be in ten years of MU films.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T12:24:46-07:00","id":1314135,"title":"","content":"I'd say he equaled or exceeded the movie version's asshole quotient (or at least lacked RDJ's charm to counterbalance it) back in 2006-2007 during the <i>Civil War</i> event. Which would have been right around the time they were developing<i> Iron Man</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-24T12:57:21-07:00","id":1314147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1308348-avengers-endgame-spoiler-thread?p=1314135#post1314135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say he equaled or exceeded the movie version's asshole quotient (or at least lacked RDJ's charm to counterbalance it) back in 2006-2007 during the <i>Civil War</i> event. Which would have been right around the time they were developing<i> Iron Man</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> His actions in that single storyline certainly didn't do him any favors. But I'd still place almost 60 years of Stark characterization vs. any of Marvel's piss-poor events over the last two decades. <br /> <br /> But hey, to each his/her own. <br /> <br /> I think they're pretty damn close, regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}